        "acorn's parser (acorn/src/expression.js) reports two errors in an object literal only once it knows the literal is not a destructuring pattern: a shorthand property with a default, as in {a = 0}, is \"Shorthand property assignments are valid only in destructuring patterns\", and a second __proto__ property is \"Redefinition of __proto__ property\". Today both errors are lost when the object literal is the object of a member expression that is itself an assignment target, although such a literal is never a pattern: with { ecmaVersion: 2022 }, parse(\"({a = 0}.x = 0);\") succeeds, and so do parse(\"[{a = 0}.x] = [];\"), parse(\"for ({a = 0}.x of []) ;\") and parse(\"({__proto__: 1, __proto__: 2}.x = 0);\"). Each must throw a SyntaxError: \"({a = 0}.x = 0);\" and \"[{a = 0}.x] = [];\" with \"Shorthand property assignments are valid only in destructuring patterns (1:4)\", \"for ({a = 0}.x of []) ;\" with the same message at (1:8), and \"({__proto__: 1, __proto__: 2}.x = 0);\" with \"Redefinition of __proto__ property (1:16)\". The same holds wherever such a literal is the object of a member expression that is assigned to or destructured into, however deep. What must not change: real destructuring patterns still parse (\"({a = 0} = {});\", \"[{a = 0}] = [];\", \"({a = 0}) => 0;\"), a member expression whose object has no such property still parses as a target (\"[{a: 0}.x] = [];\"), and the errors acorn reports today stay as they are (\"({a = 0});\" throws the shorthand message at (1:4); \"({a = 0} += 1);\" throws \"Assigning to rvalue (1:1)\"). The parser's source is in acorn/src; npm test builds it and runs the test files under test/ (the parser's expression tests are in test/tests-harmony.js, written with test() and testFail()). Add regression tests for this behaviour to the project's existing test suite. The project's tests run with npm test.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDeliverables, all required; the task is not done until each is in the tree:\n1. The implementation of the behaviour described above, in the project's own source.\n2. Regression tests: at least one new test case, in the project's own test directory and style, that fails on the current code and passes with your change, adding at least one new assertion. A change without a new test is incomplete.\n3. The visible acceptance check (node acceptance/visible/check.mjs) and the project's own test command (npm test) both passing on the final tree.\nAllowed changes: implementation code, and regression tests for the change (new test files, or new cases added to existing test files, in the project's own test directory and style).\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.\nDo not change how the project's checks run: leave the test and coverage configuration files (.taprc*, .nycrc*, .c8rc*, .mocharc*, jest.config.*, vitest.config.*, ava.config.*, karma.conf.*) and the test, pretest and posttest scripts and runner sections of package.json as they are.\nDo not delete or weaken existing tests: keep every existing assertion (it may move to another test file), add no skip, only or todo markers, and add no coverage-ignore pragmas. A change that does any of these is rejected at evaluation whatever else passes.",
